cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this protocol, pipeline or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Beyond Disease-Specific Endpoints: A Geroscience Framework for Evaluating Incretin and Glucagon Receptor Agonism Through Aging Biomarker Signatures"
abstract: >-
  A pre-specified systematic review and receptor class network meta-analysis
  protocol with its complete analysis pipeline, published before data
  extraction. Incretin based therapies modify a large share of the biomarkers
  that index biological aging, and 14 of 16 measurable markers move in the
  direction associated with slower aging, while lean mass and resting heart
  rate move the other way. This project tests whether the signature differs by
  receptor class rather than by molecule, and whether the hepatic component
  survives adjustment for accompanying weight loss. A composite Net Biological
  Age Impact Score is proposed as a weighted mean of direction adjusted
  standardized effects, together with candidate metabolic age normalization
  thresholds. No pooled estimate is reported at this stage.
